<title>GREECE: IFC SETS 27.5 BILLION GREEK DRACHMA FIVE-YEAR FRN.</title>
<headline>IFC SETS 27.5 BILLION GREEK DRACHMA FIVE-YEAR FRN.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating rate issue</p>
<p>was announced by joint lead managers Barclays Athens and Alpha</p>
<p>Credit Bank.</p>
<p>    BORROWER   INTERNATIONAL FINANCE CORPORATION</p>
<p>    AMT   27.5 BLN GRD  BASE    3M-ATHIBOR  MATURITY   27 AUG 02</p>
<p>    TYPE	 FRN	MARGIN    -75 BP    PAY DATE   27 AUG 97</p>
<p>    MOODY	AAA	ISS PRICE  PAR	FULL FEES  20 BP</p>
<p>    S&amp;P	  AAA	REOFFER    PAR</p>
<p>    LISTING    ATHENS   DENOMS (K) 1-10     SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p>    NEG PLG    NO	 CRS DFLT   YES	FORCE MAJ   STD IFC</p>
<p>    GOV LAW    GREEK    HOME CTRY  =	  TAX PROVS   NON STD</p>
<p>    MGT/UND    15 BP    SELL CONC  5 BP     PRAECIPUUM  10 BP</p>
<p>    NOTES	SENIOR, UNSECURED AND SUBORDINATED</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
